  <p>The study evaluates the intersection of the highway footprint with existing residential neighborhoods and the agricultural heritage of the Hooper area. The 2026 planning cycle is being executed with a <strong>250-foot standard footprint</strong>, designed to accommodate four travel lanes separated by a median and flanked by multi-use trails — an upgrade from the more modest 2017 Environmental Impact Statement configuration.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %}</p>
